WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.080 --> 00:00:02.340
- [Narrator] Ukraine has been targeted

00:00:02.340 --> 00:00:06.300
by barrages of Russian drones
and missiles in recent weeks.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:08.370
But a multi-layered air defense network,

00:00:08.370 --> 00:00:10.410
bolstered by many Western donations,

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.026
is allowing the country
to repel many of them.

00:00:13.026 --> 00:00:14.100
(gunshots cracking)

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:15.900
Roughly 90% of strikes in May

00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:18.453
were intercepted according
to Ukrainian officials.

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:21.720
However, some military analysts say

00:00:21.720 --> 00:00:23.540
Russia is adapting its strategy

00:00:23.540 --> 00:00:25.833
to try and evade these defenses.

00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:28.410
So as attacks intensify,

00:00:28.410 --> 00:00:30.540
here's how Kiev's air
defense systems are working

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:32.313
to intercept strikes from the sky.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.660
This video shows one of
dozens of aerial bombardments

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.613
taking place in Ukrainian cities.

00:00:39.720 --> 00:00:42.450
The Russian tactic is to
weaken Kiev's air defenses

00:00:42.450 --> 00:00:44.670
by exhausting their
supplies of ammunition.

00:00:44.670 --> 00:00:47.070
That's according to defense experts.

00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:49.830
So how is Ukraine responding
to threats from the sky?

00:00:49.830 --> 00:00:51.540
Let's take a closer look.

00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:53.910
Ukraine began the war with
an extensive stockpile

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:56.100
of Soviet-era air defense systems.

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.380
Now they're working in
tandem with weaponry

00:00:58.380 --> 00:01:00.201
supplied by Kiev's allies.

00:01:00.201 --> 00:01:03.690
That includes the US
supplied Patriot and NASAMs,

00:01:03.690 --> 00:01:05.073
and German-made Gepard.

00:01:05.910 --> 00:01:08.130
The air defense systems
follow a series of steps

00:01:08.130 --> 00:01:09.960
to take down threats.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.760
That process starts with using a radar

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:14.010
to scan the sky for incoming attacks.

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:17.310
Then if a threat is detected,
the firing system is launched

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.500
to try and blast away the projectile.

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:22.470
The Gepard system has
a range of 3.5 miles.

00:01:22.470 --> 00:01:24.360
Defense experts say it's normally used

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:25.953
against slower moving targets.

00:01:26.940 --> 00:01:28.950
In this footage, Ukrainian officials say

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:32.280
a Gepard system can be seen
targeting Russian drones.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:34.110
Military analysts say the red dots

00:01:34.110 --> 00:01:36.750
appear to be tracer rounds,
which are fired to create

00:01:36.750 --> 00:01:39.750
a trail of light towards the
target, making it more visible.

00:01:40.892 --> 00:01:43.260
While systems such as
the Gepard and NASAMs

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:46.380
can take care of low flying
cruise missiles and drones,

00:01:46.380 --> 00:01:49.470
Ukraine has struggled to
counter ballistic missiles.

00:01:49.470 --> 00:01:51.900
To target those, Ukrainian
forces have looked

00:01:51.900 --> 00:01:53.610
to the US built Patriot.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:56.040
Two of the systems were
delivered in April.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:57.840
In an interview with
the Wall Street Journal,

00:01:57.840 --> 00:01:59.850
Ukrainian president, Volodomyr Zelensky,

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:01.864
outlined its importance.

00:02:01.864 --> 00:02:06.864
(President Zelensky
speaks foreign language)

00:02:20.370 --> 00:02:22.472
- [Narrator] The sophisticated system

00:02:22.472 --> 00:02:23.305
can detect incoming threats

00:02:23.305 --> 00:02:26.040
more than 100 miles away,
and it can aim and fire

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:28.173
at identified targets within seconds.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.890
But even when Ukraine
manages to blast missiles

00:02:31.890 --> 00:02:35.100
and drones from the sky,
there are hurdles to overcome.

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:37.140
Falling debris can bring
death and destruction

00:02:37.140 --> 00:02:39.660
to residential areas,
and remaining fragments

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:40.713
can start fires.

00:02:42.090 --> 00:02:45.330
In addition, there's been
concern in Kiev and Washington

00:02:45.330 --> 00:02:48.810
over how long dwindling
ammo stocks can last.

00:02:48.810 --> 00:02:51.420
Ukrainian President Zelensky
said he's asked allies

00:02:51.420 --> 00:02:52.890
for extra support.

00:02:52.890 --> 00:02:54.330
That's as military analysts say

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:56.040
Russia is shifting its strategy,

00:02:56.040 --> 00:02:57.510
which could lead to more air strikes

00:02:57.510 --> 00:02:59.310
breaking through Ukraine's defenses.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:02.400
Techniques include flying drones at night

00:03:02.400 --> 00:03:05.583
and at a lower altitude to
try to avoid radar detection.

00:03:06.564 --> 00:03:08.550
(projectiles booming)

00:03:08.550 --> 00:03:10.740
As the war continues, air defense assets

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:14.013
could play an important role
in the counter offensive.

00:03:14.013 --> 00:03:19.013
(President Zelensky
speaks foreign language)

00:03:25.140 --> 00:03:26.430
- [Narrator] Military analysts say

00:03:26.430 --> 00:03:27.630
Ukraine will need to balance

00:03:27.630 --> 00:03:30.120
the air defense needs of
civilian infrastructure

00:03:30.120 --> 00:03:32.870
with the need to protect its
troops on the front lines.

00:03:34.260 --> 00:03:37.650
So far, neither side has been
able to take firm control

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.273
of the skies over Ukraine.

